module

public import Theory.Representation.Mathieu.SmallModules.M12Recognition.PointClassification.NormalizedInvolution.Certificate.Data

/-!
# Inputs for the two norm-row certificates

These are untrusted witness data, not norm-ideal membership theorems.
There are 7920 actual group words and 7620 proposed norm translates.
A group word is encoded by a leading binary one followed by its A/B letters.
A seed code stores eleven 13-bit indices, in the order of the powers of AB.
A translate code stores its left and right indices in two 13-bit fields.
Each combination code selects original seeds whose sum is proposed to be a
basis-column relation. The two independent certificates must prove the group
identities and the binary cancellation identities, respectively.

The exact application and reproduction command are in `source/README.md`.
Source application: Aschbacher–Smith G.7.3(2), printed p.348/PDF p.359.
-/

